From: Etna Workload <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fragment_serialize_no_encode_8e7ef60 — serializeFragment did not pct-encode

Re-injection of the bug fixed by upstream commit
8e7ef60bbb42773c2f9b93004dbfb61ab11dfe3a ("Encode fragments on
serialization"). Reversing the patch restores the buggy serializer that
emits the fragment body verbatim, breaking the round trip for any
fragment containing characters that need pct-encoding.

---
 src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
--- a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
+++ b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@

 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 serializeFragment :: Maybe ByteString -> Builder
-serializeFragment = maybe mempty (\s -> c8 '#' <> bs s)
+serializeFragment = maybe mempty (\s -> c8 '#' <> urlEncodeQuery s)

 serializeFragment' :: Maybe ByteString -> ByteString
 serializeFragment' = BB.toByteString . serializeFragment
